  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 244 PM MDT SAT OCT 17 2026\nThe closed low will slow its southern progression off the\ncentral/southern CA coast on Tuesday, as a northern trough\napproaches the BC, Canada coast. Slight cooling aloft and\nincreased cloud cover will take 3 to 5 degrees of high\ntemperatures on Tuesday. Models are showing marginally favorable\nconvective parameters over the w-central Idaho and eastern \nBoise Mtns, which are covered by a 20-30% chance of showers for \nTuesday afternoon. The closed low turns east, then northeast \nWed-Fri as it gets picked up by the northern stream trough \ntracking along the US/Canada border. Most areas see a chance of \nprecipitation during this period, through the track of the low \ncontinues to favor SW Idaho zones with the greatest coverage and\namounts. The heaviest rainfall (and mtn top snowfall) totals \nremain focused over w-central Idaho with widespread 0.25-0.50 \ninch amounts and locally up to 0.75 inches for Thur/Fri. Snow \nlevels will drop from 9-10kft MSL Wed/Thur to 6-8kft MSL on \nFriday as the wrap around precipitation ends. Friday and \nSaturday are the coolest days as the low lifts through northern \nUtah and into SE Idaho.",
